drm/msm/a6xx: Fix stale rpmh votes after suspend

Backport of the upstream fix by Shivam Rawat / Akhil P Oommen (lkml 2026-06,
"drm/msm/a6xx: Fix stale rpmh votes after suspend",
Fixes: f248d5d5159a "drm/msm/a6xx: Fix PDC sleep sequence"):
the GMU_STATUS_FW_START check in a6xx_rpmh_stop() was inverted, so the GPU RSC
was never put to sleep after the GMU firmware had run and its RPMh (BCM/ARC)
votes stayed active -> AOP never entered CXSD / DDR LPM in s2idle on X1E.
Also halt the GMU CM3 core on shutdown.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c	2026-10-02 20:46:27.080480601 +0300
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c	2026-10-02 20:47:29.746378410 +0300
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
@@ -1465,6 +1465,9 @@
 	/* Stop the interrupts and mask the hardware */
 	a6xx_gmu_irq_disable(gmu);
 
+	/* Halt the gmu cm3 core */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 1);
+
 	/* Tell RPMh to power off the GPU */
 	a6xx_rpmh_stop(gmu);
 
